-- title:
--   Degree of jmath̄(q^{Mℓ}) over the Igusa function field
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $\kappa$ a field of characteristic $p$, and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $w$ be an integral weight-one form of level $M$ over $\kappa$, that is: a modular form of weight $1$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with a power series over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose image in $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$ is the $q$-expansion (of width $1$) of that form and whose reduction `intSeriesC` in $\kappa[[q]] \subseteq \kappa((q))$ is nonzero. Write $Ig =$ `igusaFunctionFieldX1C` $\kappa\,M\,w$ for the intermediate field of $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$ generated by the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with the inverse of that reduction. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \ne p$, and put $d = \ell$ if $\ell \mid M$ and $d = \ell + 1$ otherwise. Two assertions are made. First, with $\bar\jmath(q) =$ `jqModC` $\kappa$ the reduction $q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\eta^{-24})$ of the $j$-expansion and $\bar\jmath(q^{N}) =$ `jqNModC` $\kappa\,N$ its image under $q \mapsto q^{N}$, the degree $[\,Ig(\bar\jmath(q^{M\ell})) : Ig\,]$ equals $d$. Second, there is an intermediate field $Ig'$ of $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$ whose underlying set is exactly the image of $Ig$ under the substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$, and for it $[\,Ig'(\bar\jmath(q)) : Ig'\,] = d$ as well.
--
--   This is the degree form of the statement that the $\ell$-th Hecke correspondence remains irreducible of the expected degree over the Igusa function field in characteristic $p$, in the two directions ($\alpha$ and $\beta$) of the correspondence; the generator along the first leg is $\bar\jmath(q^{M\ell})$ rather than $\bar\jmath(q^{\ell})$ because for $\ell \mid M$ one has $\Gamma_1(M) \le \Gamma_0(\ell)$, so $\bar\jmath(q^{\ell})$ already lies in the base. It is used in the construction of the Hecke roof over $X_1(Mp)$, where the residue degree of the Gauss valuation along each leg is identified with this degree.
